    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69636" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάβλα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a musical instrument of ten</i>
			or (acc. to <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				7.12.3
			</span></i>) <i>of twelve strings</i>, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				849
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ki.</u>
				10.5
			</span></i>, al.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάβλας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				Sopat.
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.3.17
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			. (Semitic word, cf. Hebr. <i>nēbel</i>;
			Phoenician, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				4.175b
			</span></i>.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> dub. sens.
			in acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν νάβλα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				175.9
			</span></i> (Egypt, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>).</div>
